russian-language-data
=====================

This repository redistributes and builds upon third-party data. Per the
CC BY-SA 4.0 ShareAlike terms, the datasets in this repository (the files under
data/) are themselves licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International (CC BY-SA 4.0) — see the LICENSE file.

Sources and attribution
-----------------------

1. OpenRussian (https://en.openrussian.org/, https://github.com/Badestrand/russian-dictionary)
   Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.
   Used to build:
     - data/stress-db.json       (word -> stress-marked form)
     - data/aspect-pairs-db.json (imperfective/perfective verb pairs)
   Changes made: the source CSV tables were parsed, filtered, deduplicated and
   reshaped into two JSON lookup files; apostrophe stress marks were converted
   to the combining acute accent (U+0301); placeholder/noise headwords were
   dropped. See scripts/build-language-db.mjs for the exact transformation.

Related projects credited by the consuming applications (not redistributed here)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. OpenCorpora (http://opencorpora.org/) — CC BY-SA — the morphological
   dictionary behind pymorphy3, queried at runtime by consumers of this data;
   its dictionary is not included in this repository.

3. pymorphy3 (https://github.com/no-plagiarism/pymorphy3) — MIT licensed code.

If you use these datasets, you must keep this attribution, indicate that changes
